These rows break the graph rule that two units able to run together never write the same file. `game-sim` and `game-shell` now both write `src/routes/s/[id]/page.view.svelte.spec.ts`: `game-sim` deletes one hand-off case and `game-shell` owns the rest. The design doc says the two can run together and that whichever merges second keeps `game-shell`'s Remix tests. Both rows state that merge rule.

Ordering them would follow the rule, but it would need an edge that names no interface row, because neither unit produces one for the other.
